# REPRODUCTION COMMANDS

Run these commands from the root of this handoff bundle.

## 1. Exact correctness replay (recommended first)

```sh
python reproducibility/run_correctness.py --output replay_receipt_new.json
```

Requirements: Python 3.10+; recorded run used Python 3.13.5. Standard library only; no network. This copies code, tests, data, and recovered legacy source into a fresh temporary directory, removes inherited `PYTHONPATH`, and executes eight independent child processes. It does not overwrite the bundled raw results.

Expected high-level result: `status = PASS`, with the core, extension, field-rank, legacy-adapter, persistence, scope-limit, and historical-contract checks passing.

## 2. Corrected v3 lifecycle timing replay

```sh
python reproducibility/run_benchmark_copy.py --output benchmark_replay_new
```

The output directory must not already exist. This copies code/data and the frozen `PROTOCOL_V3_REPLAY.json`, then runs the 38 cases in two sequential index chunks. Timing values will vary by hardware/runtime noise.

The endpoint includes build/discovery, relevant checks, serialization, actual construction of a fresh loaded instance, rechecking, and 128 executed queries. It is same-process/in-memory persistence, not cold-disk or fresh-process timing.

